    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:b04d5d61d358e759",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "dc5d37523cb462214cdd46b375c5d799c22b90188d47a89472118304ab0a4186",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-translator-20261109-mw9omcmv",
        "model": "GPT-6.1"
      },
      "text": "After breakfast, transfer to the airport for your flight to Foz do Iguaçu. On arrival, you’ll be met and taken to your hotel before visiting the falls from the Brazilian side.\n\nIguaçu Falls lies near the borders of Brazil, Argentina and Paraguay. The complex comprises 275 cascades that plunge into a deep canyon. Its best-known section is the Devil’s Throat, where the water drops up to 72 metres. Above the falls, the river flows gently, making the transition to the powerful cascades particularly striking. The falls are in a national park rich in plants and wildlife. The name ‘Iguaçu’ means ‘big water’ in Tupi-Guarani.\n\n**Optional: Macuco Safari, $125.** Start with a guided open-jeep ride of around 3 km through the rainforest, then walk to the bank of the Iguaçu River and take a motorboat to the falls.\n\n**Optional: Parque das Aves bird park, $65.** Large open-air aviaries amid tropical vegetation give birds of many species room to walk and fly freely."
